{
  "title": "Coronoid Fractures",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/trauma/1020/coronoid-fractures",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Sep 5 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Coronoid Fractures are traumatic elbow fractures that are generally pathognomonic for an episode of elbow instability.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can be made using plain radiographs of the elbow. CT studies may be helpful for surgical planning.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment may be nonoperative for nondisplaced coronoid tip fractures with a stable elbow. Surgical management is indicated for anteromedial facet fractures or fractures associated with elbow instability.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "10-15% of elbow injuries",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Types",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**isolated coronoid fracture**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "less common than previously thought",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**coronoid fracture + associated injuries**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "commonly occur with elbow dislocation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "associated with recurrent instability after dislocation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Mechanism",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "traumatic **shear injury**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "typically occurs as distal humerus is driven against coronoid with an episode of severe varus stress or posterior subluxation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "not an avulsion injury as nothing inserts on tip",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Pathoanatomy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "fractures at the coronoid base can amplify elbow instability given that",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "anterior bundle of the medial ulnar collateral ligament attaches to the sublime tubercle 18 mm distal to tip",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "anterior capsule attaches 6 mm distal to the tip of the coronoid",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**posteromedial rotatory instability**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "coronoid anteromedial facet fracture and LCL disruption",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1020/images/anteromedial%20facet%20fracture%203d%20ct.jpg",
                      "caption": "Shows an oblique anteromedial facet fracture of the coronoid."
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "results from a varus deforming force",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**posterolateral rotatory instability**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "coronoid tip fracture, radial head fracture, and LCL injury",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1020/images/coronoid%20tip%20fracture%203d%20ct.jpg",
                      "caption": "Shows a tip fracture of the coronoid."
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**Transolecranon fracture-dislocation**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "associated with a large coronoid fracture attached to the ulnar metaphysis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**Trans-ulnar basal coronoid fracture-dislocations**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "associated with a coronoid fracture that is displaced from the olecranon and ulnar metaphysis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "range of motion, patient-reported outcome measures, complication rates, and reoperation rates increased when compared to other trans-ulnar fractures.",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**terrible triad of elbow**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "coronoid fracture (transverse fracture pattern), radial head fracture, and elbow dislocation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Osteology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "coronoid tip",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "is an **intraarticular** structure",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "can be visualized during elbow arthroscopy",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "medial facet",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "important for **varus stability**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "provides insertion for the medial ulnar collateral ligament",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Biomechanics**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "coronoid functions as an **anterior buttress** of the olecranon greater sigmoid notch",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "important in preventing recurrent posterior subluxation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "primary resistor of elbow subluxation or dislocation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Classification",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "",
          "table": [
            {
              "header": true,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 3,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "**Regan and Morrey Classification**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Type I",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Coronoid process tip fracture",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1020/images/regan%20and%20morrey%20classification%20of%20coronoid%20fractures.jpg",
                          "caption": "Shows the Regan and Morrey classification of coronoid fractures."
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Type II",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Fracture of 50% or less of height",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1020/images/regan%20and%20morrey%20classification%20of%20coronoid%20fractures.jpg",
                          "caption": "Shows the Regan and Morrey classification of coronoid fractures."
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Type III",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Fracture of more than 50% of height",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1020/images/regan%20and%20morrey%20classification%20of%20coronoid%20fractures.jpg",
                          "caption": "Shows the Regan and Morrey classification of coronoid fractures."
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "",
          "table": [
            {
              "header": true,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 2,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "**O'Driscoll Classification**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "- Subdivides coronoid injuries based on location and number of coronoid fragments-Recognizes **anteromedial facet fractures** caused by varus posteromedial rotatory force",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1020/images/o'driscoll%20coronoid%20fracture%20classification.jpg",
                          "caption": "Shows the O&#39;Driscoll coronoid fracture classification."
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "elbow deformity & swelling",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "elbow pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "forearm or wrist pain may be a sign of associated injuries",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "inspection & palpation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "varus or valgus deformity",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "ecchymosis & swelling",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "diffuse tenderness",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "range of motion & instability",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "document flexion-extension and pronation-supination",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "crepitus should be noted",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**varus/valgus instability stress test**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "challenging but important for an accurate diagnosis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "neurovascular exam",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**AP and lateral elbow** views",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1020/images/anteromedial%20facet%20coronoid%20fracture%20ap%20and%20lateral%20radiographs.jpg",
                      "caption": "Show an anteromedial facet fracture of the coronoid."
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "interpretation may be difficult due to overlapping structures",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT scan",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "useful for high grade injuries and comminuted fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "brief period of immobilization, followed by early range of motion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "Type I, II, and III that are minimally displaced with **stable elbow**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "ORIF with medial approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**Type I, II, and III with persistent elbow instability**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**posteromedial rotatory instability**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "ORIF with posterior approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**indications**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**olecranon fracture dislocation**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**terrible triad of elbow**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "hinged external fixation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "large fragments",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "poor bone quality",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "difficult revision cases to help maintain stability",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**ORIF with medial approach**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "medial exposure through an interval between two heads of FCU",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "exposure more anteriorly through a split in flexor pronator mass",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "cerclage wire or No. 5 **suture through ulna drill holes for Type I injuries**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "ORIF with **retrograde cannulated screws** or plate for Type II or III injuries",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "ORIF with **buttress plate** fixation or pins and **lateral ligament repair for posteromedial rotatory instability**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1020/images/ap%20and%20lateral%20radiographs%20with%20coronoid%20fracture%20fixation.jpg",
                      "caption": "Shows coronoid fracture fixation and lateral collateral ligament repair."
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "postoperative rehabilitation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "depends on intraoperative exam following the procedure",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "thermoplastic resting splint",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "applied with elbow at 90° and forearm in neutral",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**restrict terminal 30° extension** for 2-4 weeks",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
